<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E15Xd.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2\gamma\lambda[\alpha(1-\mu_{\text{GRPO}})-(1-\mu_{\text{GRPO}})(1-\gamma)-\beta(1+\mu_{\text{GRPO}})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn> 2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mtext>GRPO</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mtext>GRPO</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mtext>GRPO</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2\gamma\lambda[\alpha(1-\mu_{\text{GRPO}})-(1-\mu_{\text{GRPO}})(1-\gamma)-\beta(1+\mu_{\text{GRPO}})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E15Xe" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E15Xe.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E15Xe.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2\gamma\lambda[2\alpha\beta-2\beta(\alpha+\beta)-\beta(2-2\beta)]{\color[rgb]{0.5,0.5,0.5}\quad\rightarrow\;\because\gamma=1-\alpha-\beta,\mu_{\text{GRPO}}=1-2\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"> 2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080" rspace="0em" stretchy="false">→</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">∵</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">γ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">α</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">β</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">μ</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">GRPO</mtext></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">β</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2\gamma\lambda[2\alpha\beta-2\beta(\alpha+\beta)-\beta(2-2\beta)]{\color[rgb]{0.5,0.5,0.5}\quad\rightarrow\;\because\gamma=1-\alpha-\beta,\mu_{\text{GRPO}}=1-2\beta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E15Xf" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E15Xf.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E15Xf.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2\gamma\lambda\cdot(-2\beta)=-4\gamma\lambda\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn> 2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2\gamma\lambda\cdot(-2\beta)=-4\gamma\lambda\beta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E15Xg" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E15Xg.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\color[rgb]{0,0,1}C}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">C</mi><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\color[rgb]{0,0,1}C}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E15Xg.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\alpha\gamma^{2}\lambda^{2}+\gamma(\gamma-1)^{2}\lambda^{2}+\beta\gamma^{2}\lambda^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\alpha\gamma^{2}\lambda^{2}+\gamma(\gamma-1)^{2}\lambda^{2}+\beta\gamma^{2}\lambda^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E15Xh" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E15Xh.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E15Xh.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(1-\gamma)\gamma^{2}\lambda^{2}+\gamma(1-\gamma)^{2}\lambda^{2}{\color[rgb]{0.5,0.5,0.5}\quad\rightarrow\;\because\gamma=1-\alpha-\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080" rspace="0em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">∵</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">γ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">α</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">β</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(1-\gamma)\gamma^{2}\lambda^{2}+\gamma(1-\gamma)^{2}\lambda^{2}{\color[rgb]{0.5,0.5,0.5}\quad\rightarrow\;\because\gamma=1-\alpha-\beta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E15Xi" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E15Xi.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E15Xi.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\gamma(1-\gamma)\lambda^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\gamma(1-\gamma)\lambda^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E15Xj" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E15Xj.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}B}+{\color[rgb]{0,0,1}C}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;" mathcolor="#BF0040">B</mi><mo>+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">C</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\color[rgb]{0.75,0,0.25}B}+{\color[rgb]{0,0,1}C}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E15Xj.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-4\gamma\lambda\beta+\gamma(1-\gamma)\lambda^{2}=\gamma\lambda(\lambda(\alpha+\beta)-4\beta){\color[rgb]{0.5,0.5,0.5}\quad\rightarrow\;\because\lambda=1-\alpha-\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080" rspace="0em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">∵</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">λ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">α</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">β</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-4\gamma\lambda\beta+\gamma(1-\gamma)\lambda^{2}=\gamma\lambda(\lambda(\alpha+\beta)-4\beta){\color[rgb]{0.5,0.5,0.5}\quad\rightarrow\;\because\lambda=1-\alpha-\beta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E15Xk" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E15Xk.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E15Xk.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lambda\gamma(1-\gamma)(\lambda-\frac{4\beta}{\alpha+\beta})=\lambda\gamma(1-\gamma)(\lambda-\frac{4}{\alpha/\beta+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lambda\gamma(1-\gamma)(\lambda-\frac{4\beta}{\alpha+\beta})=\lambda\gamma(1-\gamma)(\lambda-\frac{4}{\alpha/\beta+1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.8" class="ltx_p">Thus, <math id="A1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\text{FAPO}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mtext>FAPO</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\text{FAPO}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\text{FAPO}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mtext>FAPO</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\text{FAPO}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> can be expressed in terms of <math id="A1.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\text{GRPO}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mtext>GRPO</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\text{GRPO}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\text{GRPO}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mtext>GRPO</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\text{GRPO}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{cases}\mu_{\text{FAPO}}=\mu_{\text{GRPO}}-\lambda\gamma\\
\sigma_{\text{FAPO}}^{2}=\sigma_{\text{GRPO}}^{2}+\lambda\gamma(1-\gamma)(\lambda-\frac{4}{\alpha/\beta+1})\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mtext>FAPO</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mtext>GRPO</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mtext>FAPO</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mtext>GRPO</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{cases}\mu_{\text{FAPO}}=\mu_{\text{GRPO}}-\lambda\gamma\\
\sigma_{\text{FAPO}}^{2}=\sigma_{\text{GRPO}}^{2}+\lambda\gamma(1-\gamma)(\lambda-\frac{4}{\alpha/\beta+1})\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">When Optimization Direction Shift</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We assume a complete learning process that begins with the model unable to solve any problems, i.e., <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=1</annotation></semantics></math>.
As training progresses, <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> gradually decreases while <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> increases.
The shift in optimization direction occurs when:</p>
<table id="A1.E17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E17X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E17X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{A}_{\text{Flawed}}=\frac{1-\lambda-\mu_{\text{FAPO}}}{\sigma_{\text{FAPO}}}&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>Flawed</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mtext>FAPO</mtext></msub></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mtext>FAPO</mtext></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{A}_{\text{Flawed}}=\frac{1-\lambda-\mu_{\text{FAPO}}}{\sigma_{\text{FAPO}}}&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="5" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E17Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E17Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Leftrightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Leftrightarrow</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E17Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mu_{\text{FAPO}}&gt;1-\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mtext>FAPO</mtext></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mu_{\text{FAPO}}&gt;1-\lambda</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E17Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E17Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Leftrightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Leftrightarrow</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E17Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mu_{\text{FAPO}}=\alpha\lambda-\beta(2-\lambda)+1-\lambda&gt;1-\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mtext>FAPO</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mu_{\text{FAPO}}=\alpha\lambda-\beta(2-\lambda)+1-\lambda&gt;1-\lambda</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E17Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E17Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Leftrightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Leftrightarrow</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E17Xc.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lambda&gt;\frac{2\beta}{\alpha+\beta}=\frac{2}{\alpha/\beta+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lambda&gt;\frac{2\beta}{\alpha+\beta}=\frac{2}{\alpha/\beta+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E17Xd" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E17Xd.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Leftrightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Leftrightarrow</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E17Xd.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\alpha}{\beta}&gt;\frac{2}{\lambda}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>λ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\alpha}{\beta}&gt;\frac{2}{\lambda}-1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">How Scaling Factor Changes</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The scaling factor <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\text{FAPO}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mtext>FAPO</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\text{FAPO}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> changes over <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\text{GRPO}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mtext>GRPO</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\text{GRPO}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is:</p>
<table id="A1.E18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E18X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sigma_{\text{FAPO}}^{2}-\sigma_{\text{GRPO}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mtext>FAPO</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mtext>GRPO</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sigma_{\text{FAPO}}^{2}-\sigma_{\text{GRPO}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\lambda\gamma(1-\gamma)(\lambda-\frac{4}{\alpha/\beta+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\lambda\gamma(1-\gamma)(\lambda-\frac{4}{\alpha/\beta+1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E18Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{when }\frac{\alpha}{\beta}&lt;\frac{4}{\lambda}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>when </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mi>λ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{when }\frac{\alpha}{\beta}&lt;\frac{4}{\lambda}-1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Rightarrow\sigma_{\text{FAPO}}^{2}&lt;\sigma_{\text{GRPO}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mtext>FAPO</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>&lt;</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mtext>GRPO</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Rightarrow\sigma_{\text{FAPO}}^{2}&lt;\sigma_{\text{GRPO}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E18Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{when }\frac{\alpha}{\beta}&gt;\frac{4}{\lambda}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>when </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mi>λ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{when }\frac{\alpha}{\beta}&gt;\frac{4}{\lambda}-1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Rightarrow\sigma_{\text{FAPO}}^{2}&gt;\sigma_{\text{GRPO}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mtext>FAPO</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mtext>GRPO</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Rightarrow\sigma_{\text{FAPO}}^{2}&gt;\sigma_{\text{GRPO}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Summary: The Whole Optimization Process of FAPO</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We introduce <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=\frac{\alpha}{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=\frac{\alpha}{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> to characterize the current optimization state, which increases monotonically from <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>.
For a pre-defined and fixed <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, the learning process drives <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> upward.
Once <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> exceeds <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{2}{\lambda}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{2}{\lambda}-1</annotation></semantics></math>, the optimization direction shifts from reaching the correct answer (warm-up stage) toward reinforcing reliable reasoning (refinement stage).
As <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> continues to increase and surpasses <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{4}{\lambda}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{4}{\lambda}-1</annotation></semantics></math>, the scaling factor <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> rises accordingly, making the advantage estimation more conservative (i.e., <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\hat{A}_{\text{FAPO}}|&lt;|\hat{A}_{\text{GRPO}}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>FAPO</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>GRPO</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\hat{A}_{\text{FAPO}}|&lt;|\hat{A}_{\text{GRPO}}|</annotation></semantics></math>, for flawed-positive and fully correct rollouts).
This conservativeness helps to stabilize training by preventing overly aggressive updates, while still ensuring that correct and reliable rollouts are consistently prioritized.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Determining <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math></h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">From the above analysis, the reward assignment parameter <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> plays a central role in determining when the optimization shift is applied, whether conservative or aggressive.
In practice, we adopt a majority-guided strategy, which provides both intuitiveness and effectiveness.
In the early stage of training, when negative samples with proportion <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> dominate, flawed positives are assigned positive advantages, enabling the model to acquire the ability to produce correct answers quickly.
As training progresses and fully correct rollouts become the majority (i.e., <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&gt;\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&gt;\beta</annotation></semantics></math>), the optimization naturally shifts toward reinforcing reliable reasoning.
Formally:</p>
<table id="A1.E19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E19X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E19X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\rho_{\text{shift}}=\frac{\alpha}{\beta}=1\Rightarrow\lambda=\frac{2}{\rho_{\text{shift}}+1}=1." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mtext>shift</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mtext>shift</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\rho_{\text{shift}}=\frac{\alpha}{\beta}=1\Rightarrow\lambda=\frac{2}{\rho_{\text{shift}}+1}=1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Therefore, we set <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=1</annotation></semantics></math> as the default configuration in FAPO.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Implementation Details</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A2.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ Appendix B Implementation Details ‣ FAPO: Flawed-Aware Policy Optimization for Efficient and Reliable Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> summarizes the training configurations and hyperparameters of our generative reward model (GenRM) and final reasoning models.
For GenRM training, we follow the practice of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">An et al. (2025)</a></cite> by using a higher rollout temperature to encourage exploration.
For reasoning model training, most settings are consistent with DAPO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yu et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, except that we reduce the number of rollouts from 16 to 8 to accelerate overall training speed.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T1" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 1: </span>Training configurations and hyperparameters of our experiments.</figcaption>
<table id="A2.T1.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A2.T1.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T1.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_border_tt"></td>
